ps://haultimes.com/story/white-label-elds-expose-carriers-to-cyber-risk-e3edfb6ba9/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:33:01 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Commercial Carrier Journal</description></item><item><title>Impel Transport looking to grow its team of drivers as cross-border demand continues</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/impel-transport-looking-to-grow-its-team-of-drivers-as-cross-border-de-304b11b770/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/impel-transport-looking-to-grow-its-team-of-drivers-as-cross-border-de-304b11b770/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 10:05:12 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>PembinaValleyOnline</description></item><item><title>&#x27;It helps a lot&#x27;: Charlotte program trains aspiring truck drivers in face of national shortage, Trump restrictions</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/it-helps-a-lot-charlotte-program-trains-aspiring-truck-drivers-in-face-a9d90df6fb/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/it-helps-a-lot-charlotte-program-trains-aspiring-truck-drivers-in-face-a9d90df6fb/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>A training program run by NCIA in Charlotte currently enrolls about a dozen people in a commercial driver&#x27;s license course. The Baltimore-based group serves people who face employment barriers, and through a partnership with Transtech CDL Training, enrollees get about four weeks of instruction. People in hardship, such as food stamp recipients and survivors of domestic violence, have their license costs covered, which can otherwise run five to six thousand dollars.

The U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics projects about 214,500 openings a year over the next decade as drivers retire or leave the field. In February, Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy issued a rule that makes immigrants ineligible for CDLs when states cannot check their driving records. Duffy said the rule closes a loophole that lets non-citizens obtain CDLs with federal Employment Authorization Documents.</description></item><item><title>Truck driver shortage could affect delivery times during holidays</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/truck-driver-shortage-could-affect-delivery-times-during-holidays-cbf24c41f1/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/truck-driver-shortage-could-affect-delivery-times-during-holidays-cbf24c41f1/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 06:13:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Drivers &amp; Jobs</category><description>KING5.com</description></item><item><title>Saia plans to buy former Overnite terminal</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/saia-plans-to-buy-former-overnite-terminal-2d83b6f712/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/saia-plans-to-buy-former-overnite-terminal-2d83b6f712/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 05:04:01 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>The Gaffney Ledger</description></item><item><title>ACT Research Reports 7.4-Month Trailer Backlog Ratio</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/act-research-reports-7-4-month-trailer-backlog-ratio-ee0cf73f2d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/act-research-reports-7-4-month-trailer-backlog-ratio-ee0cf73f2d/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 04:58:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>Trucks, Parts, Service</description></item><item><title>EDITORIAL: Why Proactive Safety and Smart Efficiency Must Define Ontario Trucking’s Next Chapter</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/editorial-why-proactive-safety-and-smart-efficiency-must-define-ontari-be8983422d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/editorial-why-proactive-safety-and-smart-efficiency-must-define-ontari-be8983422d/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 02:15:47 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>In an editorial, Michael Anderson, who is stepping into the role of chair of the Ontario Trucking Association, outlined his priorities for the group. His main focus is moving truck safety oversight in Ontario toward a proactive regime. He said Transportation Minister Prabmeet Sarkaria&#x27;s recent address to members suggested the province shares that goal.

Anderson said driver training standards must keep pace as Ontario moves toward proactive enforcement. He also called for trip permits to be issued promptly, free from unnecessary bureaucratic red tape. He argued the province must not view proactive enforcement as a financial burden on the sector.</description></item><item><title>ODOT Weigh Station Operations Cite 138 Truckers</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/odot-weigh-station-operations-cite-138-truckers-1dd6c6245a/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/odot-weigh-station-operations-cite-138-truckers-1dd6c6245a/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:54:34 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Wisevoter</description></item><item><title>Calls for overpass safety crackdown as semi-trailer accidents spike</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/calls-for-overpass-safety-crackdown-as-semi-trailer-accidents-spike-d3853ba36b/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/calls-for-overpass-safety-crackdown-as-semi-trailer-accidents-spike-d3853ba36b/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:52:38 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>Global News</description></item><item><title>Winter Road Conditions Across the Midwest: How Truckers and Dispatchers Check Routes Before Departure</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/winter-road-conditions-across-the-midwest-how-truckers-and-dispatchers-e2a5d02a95/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/winter-road-conditions-across-the-midwest-how-truckers-and-dispatchers-e2a5d02a95/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:56:15 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>This Container News guide explains how drivers and dispatchers can check winter road conditions before leaving on trips through Ohio, Indiana and Kentucky. It says snow and freezing rain in Ohio can affect freight headed west hours after a driver has left, so dispatchers should build those changes into routing and scheduling. The article lists OHGO, GoKY, INDOT Traffic Wise, weather alerts and Trucker Guide camera views as tools for checking routes.

The article notes that state crews do not maintain county, township or city roads, so the final miles to a delivery site may not be clear even when the highway is. It also cautions that traffic cameras show only specific spots and do not replace official reports of closures, crashes or restrictions. Dispatchers are advised to keep tracking conditions after departure and to put safety ahead of on-time arrival if a route turns hazardous.</description></item><item><title>Moraine Park Adds CDL Training Track in Horicon, WI</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/moraine-park-adds-cdl-training-track-in-horicon-wi-46294a6900/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/moraine-park-adds-cdl-training-track-in-horicon-wi-46294a6900/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:47:24 +0000</pubDate><category>Drivers &amp; Jobs</category><description>Hoodline</description></item><item><title>14 Arrested in $22.5M SoCal Cargo Theft Case</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/14-arrested-in-22-5m-socal-cargo-theft-case-60dbe22861/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/14-arrested-in-22-5m-socal-cargo-theft-case-60dbe22861/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:00:54 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Palisades News</description></item><item><title>Five Convicted in $1.5 Million Philadelphia Cargo Theft Ring</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/five-convicted-in-1-5-million-philadelphia-cargo-theft-ring-ef1c11a5c8/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/five-convicted-in-1-5-million-philadelphia-cargo-theft-ring-ef1c11a5c8/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 13:11:10 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>MyChesCo</description></item><item><title>Borderlands Mexico: Truckers secure 29 agreements on highway safety after nationwide strike</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/borderlands-mexico-truckers-secure-29-agreements-on-highway-safety-aft-72339a475b/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/borderlands-mexico-truckers-secure-29-agreements-on-highway-safety-aft-72339a475b/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Drivers &amp; Jobs</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Road Truckers: New Beginning PC Release Window Set for Q1 2027</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/road-truckers-new-beginning-pc-release-window-set-for-q1-2027-b4a5097484/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/road-truckers-new-beginning-pc-release-window-set-for-q1-2027-b4a5097484/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 09:55:47 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>The Globe and Mail</description></item><item><title>Shippers’ backup plan is getting more expensive</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/shippers-backup-plan-is-getting-more-expensive-7737447226/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/shippers-backup-plan-is-getting-more-expensive-7737447226/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:30:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Alberta proposes $50K fines for unsafe trucking operators, public naming of offenders</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/alberta-proposes-50k-fines-for-unsafe-trucking-operators-public-naming-a9b17e458a/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/alberta-proposes-50k-fines-for-unsafe-trucking-operators-public-naming-a9b17e458a/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:47:17 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Truck News</description></item><item><title>Driver on an ABN at 56 cents a kilometre was an employee, not a subcontractor, of a Melbourne trucking company</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/driver-on-an-abn-at-56-cents-a-kilometre-was-an-employee-not-a-subcont-c30d35c995/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/driver-on-an-abn-at-56-cents-a-kilometre-was-an-employee-not-a-subcont-c30d35c995/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:30:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>onnotice.com.au</description></item><item><title>Trucker who crashed off Pascagoula River Bridge identified, cause still unknown</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/trucker-who-crashed-off-pascagoula-river-bridge-identified-cause-still-b2f2c94508/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/trucker-who-crashed-off-pascagoula-river-bridge-identified-cause-still-b2f2c94508/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:59:46 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>A tractor-trailer driver, identified as 64-year-old Norberto Barahona-Mejia of Conroe, Texas, died after his truck left the Pascagoula River Bridge on I-10 in Jackson County, Mississippi, on November 17. According to a report citing WKRG, the crash happened around 12:15 a.m., after the truck collided with a Honda Accord that was also eastbound, and the trailer went over the side of the bridge into the water below. The 27-year-old driver of the Honda Accord and a 28-year-old passenger were injured and are expected to make full recoveries. Officials are still investigating, and the cause has not been released.</description></item><item><title>PS Logistics Acquires East Tennessee Trucking Firm</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/ps-logistics-acquires-east-tennessee-trucking-firm-955ef499f1/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/ps-logistics-acquires-east-tennessee-trucking-firm-955ef499f1/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:49:08 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Wisevoter</description></item><item><title>21-year-old allegedly led $22.5 million train cargo theft scheme in California</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/21-year-old-allegedly-led-22-5-million-train-cargo-theft-scheme-in-cal-71bc33b849/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/21-year-old-allegedly-led-22-5-million-train-cargo-theft-scheme-in-cal-71bc33b849/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:40:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Modern Ghana</description></item><item><title>Bot Auto launches ‘Capacity Grid’ with agreements for 200 million miles of driverless trucking</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/bot-auto-launches-capacity-grid-with-agreements-for-200-million-miles-6c016a9026/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/bot-auto-launches-capacity-grid-with-agreements-for-200-million-miles-6c016a9026/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:09:14 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>Bot Auto has launched Capacity Grid, a network intended to match shipper and broker demand with driverless trucking capacity, and has signed agreements covering 200 million miles of driverless freight operations. Customers can reserve capacity for set routes and time windows at agreed prices, buying transportation by the mile without owning trucks. FreightVana, a logistics company specializing in power-only freight transportation, has a commitment covering 50 million miles.

The company said a driverless load ran from northeast Houston to Hutchins, near Dallas, on April 29, covering 231 miles for Ryan Transportation. Figures reported by the company put the driverless trip at $1.89 per mile, against $3.78 for a comparable human-driven operation within its business. Bot Auto has not specified when the full 200 million miles will be completed.</description></item><item><title>DHL Express makes customs clearance easier for small cross-border shippers</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/dhl-express-makes-customs-clearance-easier-for-small-cross-border-ship-cfd66d1192/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/dhl-express-makes-customs-clearance-easier-for-small-cross-border-ship-cfd66d1192/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:38:56 +0000</pubDate><category>Cross-Border</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Supply Chain Analyst in Dearborn, MI for Penske Truck Leasing</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/supply-chain-analyst-in-dearborn-mi-for-penske-truck-leasing-5487a067b6/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/supply-chain-analyst-in-dearborn-mi-for-penske-truck-leasing-5487a067b6/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:51:06 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Transport Topics</description></item><item><title>Lost Father In Class 10, Truck Driver&#x27;s Son Becomes DSP In Jammu And Kashmir</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/lost-father-in-class-10-truck-driver-s-son-becomes-dsp-in-jammu-and-ka-f2da14dc5d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/lost-father-in-class-10-truck-driver-s-son-becomes-dsp-in-jammu-and-ka-f2da14dc5d/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:53:32 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>NDTV</description></item><item><title>CH Robinson Slams RICO Claims That It Used &#x27;Illegal&#x27; Carriers</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/ch-robinson-slams-rico-claims-that-it-used-illegal-c